docs/prd/06-views.md:163:  ↓ 4 Match (Model): The model does not read the original item. Show each existing thesis's subject, question, focus, ladder, due date and open/closed state. In one call: (1) decide candidate identity or a narrower part, succession with unchanged ladder orientation but new thresholds, new thesis for distinct or merely similar questions, or skip overly broad questions, numbers beyond this/next year and the same period of a closed thesis; give reasons; (2) choose dependencies and directions among searched, block-5 and same-item new theses; (3) compare evidence linked only to existing theses. Evidence linked to candidates waits for their destinations, then searches all linked existing theses together and uses one further comparison call. Evidence linked only to new theses is new evidence.
docs/prd/06-views.md:176:| Succession | The next period of the same focus: the next year for numbers, or continued tracking after an event thesis closed | Create a thesis and record succession |
